module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.KoszulGlobalSectionsAnnihilation
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.CechContractible
public import
  StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.KoszulSectionsProjection
public import StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedComplete.NoetherianKoszulProIso
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Tor.AlmostFlatResolution

/-!
# Multiplication by a monomial is null-homotopic on a constant Koszul system

Let `𝒜` be a preadditive category with finite products, let `Y` be an object of `𝒜` and let
`σ : (Fin r → ℕ) → End Y` be multiplicative — `σ 0 = 𝟙` and `σ e ≫ σ e' = σ (e + e')`. The
*constant Koszul system* of `σ` at level `n` is the diagram on the poset of subsets of `Fin r`
which is constant at `Y` and whose transition map along `S ⊆ T` is `σ` of the exponent vector
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulExp n S T`, that is the monomial with exponent `n + 1` at
the indices of `T ∖ S`. Its alternating Čech complex is the Koszul complex on the `(n+1)`-st
powers, in the grading of [Stacks, Tag 0913]: the degree-`p` term is the product of copies of
`Y` indexed by the subsets of cardinality `p`.

This file proves that `σ` of the exponent vector concentrated at a single index `j` is
null-homotopic on that complex, which is [Stacks, Tag 0663] in the generality shared by the two
Koszul systems the library already has: `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulPowerFunctorOn`, the
Koszul system with coefficients in a sheaf of modules on a ringed site, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleKoszulPowerFunctor`, the same construction for a module over
a commutative ring. Both are *definitionally* the constant Koszul system of their own monomial
multiplication, so the null-homotopy transfers to each of them by `rfl`.

The second half of the file draws the consequence over a commutative ring: the Artin–Rees input
of [Stacks, Tag 0921] with coefficients, in the subset-product model and in the elementary
cocycle-into-coboundary form that a flat base change inherits.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.constSystem` — the constant Koszul system of `σ` at level `n`.
* `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.constSmulTerm` and
  `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.constSmulMap` — multiplication by the monomial `σ e` on the
  degree-`p` term and on the whole complex.
* `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.constHtpy` — the contracting homotopy at an index `j`.
* `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.constDownNat` and
  `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.constDownMap` — the transition from the `(m+1)`-st down to the
  `(n+1)`-st Koszul powers, at a subset `S` the monomial `f_{Sᶜ}^{m-n}`.
* `CategoryTheory.Limits.Pi.biproductIota` — the inclusion of a factor into a finite product.
* `Stacks.KoszulProZero.modComplex` and `Stacks.KoszulProZero.modDown` — the Koszul complex on
  the `(n+1)`-st powers with coefficients in a module, and its downward transition.
  Definitionally `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleKoszulPowerComplex`.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.constHtpy_comp_dAux_add_dAux_comp_constHtpy` — the homotopy
  identity `h ∘ d + d ∘ h = σ (singleExp j n)`.
* `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.constSmulNullHomotopic` — **multiplication by the monomial
  `f_j^{n+1}` is null-homotopic on the Koszul complex on the `(n+1)`-st powers.**
* `CategoryTheory.Limits.Pi.total_biproductIota` — the identity of a finite product is the sum of
  the composites projection-inclusion.
* `Stacks.KoszulProZero.range_le_ideal_smul_of_total` — a map of modules whose components are
  scalars from an ideal has its range inside that ideal times the target.
* `Stacks.KoszulProZero.span_le_annihilator_homology_modComplex` — **[Stacks, Tag 0663] with
  coefficients, in the subset-product model**: over a commutative ring the ideal generated by
  `a_1^{n+1}, …, a_r^{n+1}` annihilates every cohomology module of the Koszul complex on those
  powers with coefficients in a module.
* `Stacks.KoszulProZero.range_modDown_le_ideal_smul` — in a degree below the top degree `r` the
  image of the downward transition lies in `Jᵏ` times the term.
* `Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_modDown_cocyclesIntoCoboundaries` — **the Artin–Rees input with
  coefficients**: over a Noetherian ring, for a finite module, in every degree `p < r` and at
  every level `n` there is a later level `m` whose downward transition carries the cocycles of
  level `m` into the coboundaries of level `n`.

## Implementation notes

The construction and the proof of the homotopy identity are those of
`Stacks.Sheaves.KoszulGlobalSections.koszulSmulNullHomotopic`, which is the same statement for
the Koszul system *without coefficients* on a site. That file cannot be specialised to this one,
nor this one to it: there the scalars are global sections of a sheaf of rings acting through
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd`, a natural endomorphism of the identity functor of
the category of modules, whereas here they are an abstract multiplicative family of
endomorphisms of a single object, which is what a module over a commutative ring supplies and
what makes the statement available with coefficients. Deriving both from one statement would ask
for the category of sheaves of modules to be `CategoryTheory.Linear` over the global sections of
its sheaf of rings, which Mathlib does not provide.

Because every object of the system is the same `Y`, the component of the homotopy at a subset
`A` is a bare projection onto the factor indexed by `A ∪ {j}`: no transition map has to be
inverted, unlike in `CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech.hAux`, the contracting homotopy of the
extended alternating Čech complex.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0663](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0663)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0913](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0913)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

universe u v

namespace CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech

/-! ## The constant Koszul system of a multiplicative family of monomials -/

section ConstSystem

variable {r : ℕ} {𝒜 : Type u} [Category.{v} 𝒜] [Preadditive 𝒜] [HasFiniteProducts 𝒜]
  {Y : 𝒜} (σ : (Fin r → ℕ) → (Y ⟶ Y))
  (hσ0 : σ 0 = 𝟙 Y) (hσadd : ∀ e e', σ e ≫ σ e' = σ (e + e'))

/-- The exponent vector carrying the exponent `n + 1` at the single index `j`. It is the
exponent of a transition map of a Koszul system across one new index. -/
def singleExp (j : Fin r) (n : ℕ) : Fin r → ℕ := fun i => if i = j then n + 1 else 0

/-- **The constant Koszul system of a multiplicative family of monomials.** The diagram on the
poset of subsets of `Fin r` which is constant at `Y` and whose transition map along `S ⊆ T` is
the monomial with exponent `n + 1` at the indices of `T ∖ S`.

Reducible, as `Stacks.Sheaves.KoszulGlobalSections.koszulFunctor` is and for the same reason: the
components of the contracting homotopy below are bare projections, whose type mentions the value
of the system at a subset, and they have to be composable with endomorphisms of `Y` without an
`eqToHom`. -/
@[reducible] def constSystem (n : ℕ) : Finset (Fin r) ⥤ 𝒜 where
  obj _ := Y
  map {S T} _ := σ (koszulExp n S T)
  map_id S := by
    rw [koszulExp_self]
    exact hσ0
  map_comp {S T V} g g' := by
    rw [hσadd, koszulExp_add (leOfHom g) (leOfHom g')]

omit [Preadditive 𝒜] [HasFiniteProducts 𝒜] in
/-- The constant Koszul system takes the value `Y` at every subset. -/
@[simp]
theorem constSystem_obj (n : ℕ) (S : Finset (Fin r)) :
    (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S = Y :=
  rfl

omit [Preadditive 𝒜] [HasFiniteProducts 𝒜] in
/-- The transition map of the constant Koszul system along `S ⊆ T` is `σ (koszulExp n S T)`. -/
theorem constSystem_map (n : ℕ) {S T : Finset (Fin r)} (g : S ⟶ T) :
    (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).map g = σ (koszulExp n S T) :=
  rfl

omit [Preadditive 𝒜] [HasFiniteProducts 𝒜] in
/-- A transition map of the constant Koszul system across a single new index `k` is the monomial
concentrated at `k`. -/
theorem constSystem_map_single (n : ℕ) {S T : Finset (Fin r)} (h : S ⊆ T) {k : Fin r}
    (hk : T \ S = {k}) :
    (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).map (homOfLE h) = σ (singleExp k n) := by
  refine congrArg σ (funext fun i => ?_)
  simp [koszulExp, singleExp, hk]

/-- **Multiplication by the monomial `σ e`, as an endomorphism of the constant Koszul system.**
It is a morphism of systems because monomials commute. -/
def constSmulNat (n : ℕ) (e : Fin r → ℕ) :
    constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n ⟶ constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n where
  app _ := σ e
  naturality {S T} _ := by
    change σ (koszulExp n S T) ≫ σ e = σ e ≫ σ (koszulExp n S T)
    rw [hσadd, hσadd, add_comm]

omit [Preadditive 𝒜] [HasFiniteProducts 𝒜] in
/-- The component of `constSmulNat` at every subset is `σ e`. -/
@[simp]
theorem constSmulNat_app (n : ℕ) (e : Fin r → ℕ) (S : Finset (Fin r)) :
    (constSmulNat σ hσ0 hσadd n e).app S = σ e :=
  rfl

/-- **Multiplication by the monomial `σ e` on the degree-`p` term** of the Koszul complex: the
product over the subsets of cardinality `p` of copies of `σ e`. -/
def constSmulTerm (n : ℕ) (e : Fin r → ℕ) (p : ℤ) :
    term (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) p ⟶ term (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) p :=
  mapX (constSmulNat σ hσ0 hσadd n e) p

omit [Preadditive 𝒜] in
/-- Each component of `constSmulTerm` is the projection followed by `σ e`. -/
@[simp]
theorem constSmulTerm_comp_pi (n : ℕ) (e : Fin r → ℕ) (p : ℤ) (A : Idx r p) :
    constSmulTerm σ hσ0 hσadd n e p ≫
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) A =
      Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) A ≫ σ e :=
  mapX_comp_pi (constSmulNat σ hσ0 hσadd n e) A

/-- **Multiplication by the monomial `σ e`, as an endomorphism of the Koszul complex.** -/
def constSmulMap (n : ℕ) (e : Fin r → ℕ) :
    complex (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) ⟶ complex (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) :=
  map (constSmulNat σ hσ0 hσadd n e)

/-- The degree-`p` component of `constSmulMap` is `constSmulTerm`. -/
@[simp]
theorem constSmulMap_f (n : ℕ) (e : Fin r → ℕ) (p : ℤ) :
    (constSmulMap σ hσ0 hσadd n e).f p = constSmulTerm σ hσ0 hσadd n e p :=
  rfl

end ConstSystem

/-! ## The contracting homotopy -/

section Homotopy

variable {r : ℕ} {𝒜 : Type u} [Category.{v} 𝒜] [Preadditive 𝒜] [HasFiniteProducts 𝒜]
  {Y : 𝒜} (σ : (Fin r → ℕ) → (Y ⟶ Y))
  (hσ0 : σ 0 = 𝟙 Y) (hσadd : ∀ e e', σ e ≫ σ e' = σ (e + e')) (j : Fin r) (n : ℕ)

/-- **The contracting homotopy of the constant Koszul system at the index `j`.** Its component
at a subset `A` of cardinality `q` is the projection onto the factor indexed by `A ∪ {j}`, with
the sign with which `j` enters `A ∪ {j}`, and is zero when `j` already lies in `A`. -/
def constHtpy {p q : ℤ} (hqp : q + 1 = p) :
    term (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) p ⟶ term (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) q :=
  Pi.lift fun A : Idx r q =>
    if hA : j ∈ A.1 then 0
    else Cech.cechSign A.1 j •
      Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) (idxInsert j A hA hqp)

/-- The component of the homotopy at a subset containing `j` vanishes. -/
theorem constHtpy_comp_pi_of_mem {p q : ℤ} (hqp : q + 1 = p) (A : Idx r q) (hA : j ∈ A.1) :
    constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp ≫
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r q => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) A = 0 := by
  rw [constHtpy, Pi.lift_comp_π, dite_eq_left hA]

/-- The component of the homotopy at a subset not containing `j`. -/
theorem constHtpy_comp_pi_of_notMem {p q : ℤ} (hqp : q + 1 = p) (A : Idx r q) (hA : j ∉ A.1) :
    constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp ≫
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r q => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) A =
      Cech.cechSign A.1 j •
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1)
          (idxInsert j A hA hqp) := by
  rw [constHtpy, Pi.lift_comp_π, dite_eq_right hA]

/-- The component of the homotopy at a subset not containing `j`, read on a factor whose index
is only propositionally `A ∪ {j}`. -/
theorem constHtpy_comp_pi_of_eq {p q : ℤ} (hqp : q + 1 = p) (A : Idx r q) (hA : j ∉ A.1)
    (B : Idx r p) (hBA : B.1 = insert j A.1) :
    constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp ≫
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r q => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) A =
      Cech.cechSign A.1 j •
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) B := by
  rw [constHtpy_comp_pi_of_notMem σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp A hA]
  congr 2
  exact Subtype.ext hBA.symm

/-- The homotopy followed by the differential, read on the factor indexed by `B`. -/
private theorem constHtpy_comp_dAux_comp_pi {p q : ℤ} (hqp : q + 1 = p) (B : Idx r p) :
    constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp ≫ dAux (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) hqp ≫
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) B =
      ∑ k ∈ B.1.attach, Cech.cechSign B.1 k.1 •
        ((constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp ≫
            Pi.π (fun S : Idx r q => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1)
              (idxErase B k hqp)) ≫
          (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).map
            (homOfLE (Finset.erase_subset (k : Fin r) B.1))) := by
  rw [dAux_comp_pi (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) hqp B, Preadditive.comp_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ => ?_
  rw [Preadditive.comp_zsmul, ← Category.assoc]

/-- The homotopy followed by the differential, read on the factor indexed by a subset `B`
containing `j`, is multiplication by the monomial concentrated at `j`. -/
private theorem constHtpy_comp_dAux_comp_pi_of_mem {p q : ℤ} (hqp : q + 1 = p) (B : Idx r p)
    (hB : j ∈ B.1) :
    constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp ≫ dAux (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) hqp ≫
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) B =
      Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) B ≫ σ (singleExp j n) := by
  classical
  have hzero : ∀ b ∈ B.1.attach, b ≠ (⟨j, hB⟩ : {x // x ∈ B.1}) →
      Cech.cechSign B.1 b.1 • ((constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp ≫
          Pi.π (fun S : Idx r q => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1)
            (idxErase B b hqp)) ≫
        (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).map
          (homOfLE (Finset.erase_subset (b : Fin r) B.1))) = 0 := by
    intro b _ hb
    have hjb : j ∈ (idxErase B b hqp).1 := by
      rw [val_idxErase]
      exact Finset.mem_erase.mpr ⟨fun h => hb (Subtype.ext h.symm), hB⟩
    rw [constHtpy_comp_pi_of_mem σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp _ hjb, zero_comp, smul_zero]
  have hA : j ∉ (idxErase B (⟨j, hB⟩ : {x // x ∈ B.1}) hqp).1 := by
    rw [val_idxErase]
    exact Finset.notMem_erase j B.1
  rw [constHtpy_comp_dAux_comp_pi σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp B,
    Finset.sum_eq_single_of_mem (⟨j, hB⟩ : {x // x ∈ B.1}) (Finset.mem_attach _ _) hzero,
    constHtpy_comp_pi_of_eq σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp _ hA B (by
      rw [val_idxErase]
      exact (Finset.insert_erase hB).symm),
    Preadditive.zsmul_comp, smul_smul,
    show Cech.cechSign B.1 ((⟨j, hB⟩ : {x // x ∈ B.1}) : Fin r) *
          Cech.cechSign ((idxErase B (⟨j, hB⟩ : {x // x ∈ B.1}) hqp).1) j = 1 by
      rw [val_idxErase, Cech.cechSign_erase]
      exact cechSign_mul_self B.1 j,
    one_smul]
  congr 1
  exact constSystem_map_single σ hσ0 hσadd n _ (Finset.sdiff_erase_self hB)

/-- The homotopy followed by the differential, read on the factor indexed by a subset `B` not
containing `j`, as a signed sum over the elements of `B`. -/
private theorem constHtpy_comp_dAux_comp_pi_of_notMem {p q : ℤ} (hqp : q + 1 = p)
    (B : Idx r p) (hjmem : ∀ k : {x // x ∈ B.1}, j ∉ (idxErase B k hqp).1) :
    constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp ≫ dAux (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) hqp ≫
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) B =
      ∑ k ∈ B.1.attach, (Cech.cechSign B.1 k.1 * Cech.cechSign (B.1.erase k.1) j) •
        (Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1)
            (idxInsert j (idxErase B k hqp) (hjmem k) hqp) ≫ σ (singleExp k.1 n)) := by
  classical
  rw [constHtpy_comp_dAux_comp_pi σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp B]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ => ?_
  rw [constHtpy_comp_pi_of_notMem σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp _ (hjmem k),
    Preadditive.zsmul_comp, smul_smul,
    show Cech.cechSign B.1 (k : Fin r) *
          Cech.cechSign ((idxErase B k hqp).1) j =
        Cech.cechSign B.1 (k : Fin r) * Cech.cechSign (B.1.erase (k : Fin r)) j by
      rw [val_idxErase]]
  congr 2
  exact constSystem_map_single σ hσ0 hσadd n _ (Finset.sdiff_erase_self k.2)

/-- The differential followed by the homotopy, read on the factor indexed by a subset `B` not
containing `j`: multiplication by the monomial at `j` plus a signed sum over the elements
of `B`. -/
private theorem dAux_comp_constHtpy_comp_pi_of_notMem {p q s : ℤ} (hqp : q + 1 = p)
    (hps : p + 1 = s) (B : Idx r p) (hB : j ∉ B.1)
    (hjmem : ∀ k : {x // x ∈ B.1}, j ∉ (idxErase B k hqp).1)
    (T : Idx r s) (hTB : T.1 = insert j B.1) :
    dAux (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) hps ≫ constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hps ≫
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) B =
      (Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) B ≫
          σ (singleExp j n)) +
        ∑ k ∈ B.1.attach, (Cech.cechSign B.1 j * Cech.cechSign (insert j B.1) k.1) •
          (Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1)
              (idxInsert j (idxErase B k hqp) (hjmem k) hqp) ≫ σ (singleExp k.1 n)) := by
  classical
  have hTj : T.1.erase j = B.1 := by rw [hTB, Finset.erase_insert hB]
  have hTk : ∀ k : {x // x ∈ B.1}, T.1.erase k.1 = insert j (B.1.erase k.1) := fun k => by
    rw [hTB]
    exact Finset.erase_insert_of_ne (fun h : j = k.1 => hB (h ▸ k.2))
  rw [constHtpy_comp_pi_of_eq σ hσ0 hσadd j n hps B hB T hTB, Preadditive.comp_zsmul,
    dAux_comp_pi (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) hps T, Finset.smul_sum,
    sum_attach_insert_of_eq hTB hB]
  have hsignj : Cech.cechSign B.1 j * Cech.cechSign T.1 j = 1 := by
    rw [hTB, Cech.cechSign_insert]
    exact cechSign_mul_self B.1 j
  have hsignk : ∀ k : Fin r, Cech.cechSign T.1 k = Cech.cechSign (insert j B.1) k :=
    fun k => by rw [hTB]
  have hEsub : ∀ m : {x // x ∈ T.1}, (idxErase T m hps).1 ⊆ T.1 := fun m => by
    rw [val_idxErase]
    exact Finset.erase_subset _ _
  have key : ∀ m : {x // x ∈ T.1},
      Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) (idxErase T m hps) ≫
          (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).map (homOfLE (hEsub m)) =
        Pi.π (fun S : Idx r p => (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n).obj S.1) (idxErase T m hps) ≫
          σ (singleExp m.1 n) := fun m => by
    rw [constSystem_map_single σ hσ0 hσadd n (hEsub m) (k := m.1)
      (by rw [val_idxErase]; exact Finset.sdiff_erase_self m.2)]
  congr 1
  · rw [key, show idxErase T (⟨j, hTB ▸ Finset.mem_insert_self j B.1⟩ : {x // x ∈ T.1}) hps = B from
      Subtype.ext (by rw [val_idxErase, hTj]), smul_smul, hsignj, one_smul]
  · refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun k _ => ?_
    rw [key, show idxErase T (⟨k.1, hTB ▸ Finset.mem_insert_of_mem k.2⟩ : {x // x ∈ T.1}) hps =
        idxInsert j (idxErase B k hqp) (hjmem k) hqp from
      Subtype.ext (by rw [val_idxErase, hTk k, val_idxInsert, val_idxErase]), smul_smul, hsignk]

/-- **The homotopy identity.** In each degree, multiplication by the monomial concentrated at
`j` is the sum of the two composites of the differential with the contracting homotopy at
`j`. -/
theorem constHtpy_comp_dAux_add_dAux_comp_constHtpy {p q s : ℤ} (hqp : q + 1 = p)
    (hps : p + 1 = s) :
    constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp ≫ dAux (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) hqp +
        dAux (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) hps ≫ constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n hps =
      constSmulTerm σ hσ0 hσadd n (singleExp j n) p := by
  classical
  refine Pi.hom_ext _ _ fun B => ?_
  rw [Preadditive.add_comp, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, constSmulTerm_comp_pi]
  by_cases hB : j ∈ B.1
  · rw [constHtpy_comp_pi_of_mem σ hσ0 hσadd j n hps B hB, comp_zero, add_zero]
    exact constHtpy_comp_dAux_comp_pi_of_mem σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp B hB
  · have hjmem : ∀ k : {x // x ∈ B.1}, j ∉ (idxErase B k hqp).1 := fun k h => by
      rw [val_idxErase] at h
      exact hB (Finset.mem_of_mem_erase h)
    rw [constHtpy_comp_dAux_comp_pi_of_notMem σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp B hjmem,
      dAux_comp_constHtpy_comp_pi_of_notMem σ hσ0 hσadd j n hqp hps B hB hjmem
        (idxInsert j B hB hps) rfl,
      show ∀ (Z : 𝒜) (a b c : term (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) p ⟶ Z),
          a + (b + c) = (a + c) + b from
        fun _ a b c => by rw [add_comm b c, ← add_assoc], ← Finset.sum_add_distrib,
      Finset.sum_eq_zero (fun k _ => by
        rw [← add_smul, cechSign_erase_add_cechSign_insert k.2 hB, zero_smul]),
      zero_add]

/-- **Multiplication by the monomial `f_j^{n+1}` is null-homotopic on the Koszul complex on the
`(n+1)`-st powers**: the contracting homotopy at `j` realises it. This is [Stacks, Tag 0663] for
a constant Koszul system. -/
def constSmulNullHomotopic :
    Homotopy (constSmulMap σ hσ0 hσadd n (singleExp j n)) 0 :=
  (CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.equivHomotopy _ _).symm
    ⟨CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.mk
      (fun p q _ => constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n (show q + 1 = p by omega)), by
      ext p : 1
      rw [CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.ofHom_v,
        CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.add_v,
        CochainComplex.HomComplex.δ_v (-1) 0 (neg_add_cancel 1) _ p p (add_zero p) (p - 1)
          (p + 1) rfl rfl]
      simp only [CochainComplex.HomComplex.Cochain.ofHom_v, Int.negOnePow_zero, one_smul,
        HomologicalComplex.zero_f, add_zero, constSmulMap_f]
      rw [complex_d_eq (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) (show p - 1 + 1 = p by omega),
        complex_d_eq (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) rfl]
      exact (constHtpy_comp_dAux_add_dAux_comp_constHtpy σ hσ0 hσadd j n
        (show p - 1 + 1 = p by omega) rfl).symm⟩

end Homotopy

/-! ## The transition from a higher to a lower Koszul power -/

section Down

variable {r : ℕ} {𝒜 : Type u} [Category.{v} 𝒜] [Preadditive 𝒜] [HasFiniteProducts 𝒜]
  {Y : 𝒜} (σ : (Fin r → ℕ) → (Y ⟶ Y))
  (hσ0 : σ 0 = 𝟙 Y) (hσadd : ∀ e e', σ e ≫ σ e' = σ (e + e'))

/-- The exponent vector of the transition from the `(m+1)`-st to the `(n+1)`-st Koszul powers at
a subset `S`: the exponent `m - n` at every index *outside* `S`. -/
def downExp (m n : ℕ) (S : Finset (Fin r)) : Fin r → ℕ := fun i => if i ∈ S then 0 else m - n

/-- **The morphism of constant Koszul systems from the `(m+1)`-st down to the `(n+1)`-st
powers.** At a subset `S` it is the monomial `f_{Sᶜ}^{m-n}`. The exponent is on the complement
of `S` because the differential raises the cardinality, so a factor of the degree-`p` term is
indexed by the subset of the `f_i` that have *not* yet been contracted. -/
def constDownNat {m n : ℕ} (hnm : n ≤ m) :
    constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd m ⟶ constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n where
  app S := σ (downExp m n S)
  naturality {S T} g := by
    change σ (koszulExp m S T) ≫ σ (downExp m n T) = σ (downExp m n S) ≫ σ (koszulExp n S T)
    rw [hσadd, hσadd]
    refine congrArg σ (funext fun i => ?_)
    by_cases hiS : i ∈ S
    · simp [koszulExp, downExp, Finset.mem_sdiff, hiS, leOfHom g hiS]
    · by_cases hiT : i ∈ T
      · simp only [koszulExp, downExp, Finset.mem_sdiff, hiS, hiT, Pi.add_apply, ite_true,
          ite_false, and_true, not_false_eq_true]
        omega
      · simp [koszulExp, downExp, Finset.mem_sdiff, hiS, hiT, Pi.add_apply]

omit [Preadditive 𝒜] [HasFiniteProducts 𝒜] in
/-- The component of `constDownNat` at a subset `S` is `σ (downExp m n S)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem constDownNat_app {m n : ℕ} (hnm : n ≤ m) (S : Finset (Fin r)) :
    (constDownNat σ hσ0 hσadd hnm).app S = σ (downExp m n S) :=
  rfl

/-- **The transition map of Koszul complexes from the `(m+1)`-st down to the `(n+1)`-st
powers.** -/
def constDownMap {m n : ℕ} (hnm : n ≤ m) :
    complex (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd m) ⟶ complex (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) :=
  map (constDownNat σ hσ0 hσadd hnm)

/-- The degree-`p` component of `constDownMap` is the map induced by `constDownNat` on the
degree-`p` term. -/
@[simp]
theorem constDownMap_f {m n : ℕ} (hnm : n ≤ m) (p : ℤ) :
    (constDownMap σ hσ0 hσadd hnm).f p = mapX (constDownNat σ hσ0 hσadd hnm) p :=
  rfl

omit [Preadditive 𝒜] [HasFiniteProducts 𝒜] in
/-- **The downward transitions compose.** Going down from the `(m₂+1)`-st to the `(m₁+1)`-st and
then to the `(n+1)`-st powers is going down from the `(m₂+1)`-st to the `(n+1)`-st, because the
exponents `m₂ - m₁` and `m₁ - n` add to `m₂ - n`. -/
theorem constDownNat_comp {m₁ m₂ n : ℕ} (h₁ : m₁ ≤ m₂) (h₂ : n ≤ m₁) :
    constDownNat σ hσ0 hσadd h₁ ≫ constDownNat σ hσ0 hσadd h₂ =
      constDownNat σ hσ0 hσadd (h₂.trans h₁) := by
  refine NatTrans.ext (funext fun S => ?_)
  change σ (downExp m₂ m₁ S) ≫ σ (downExp m₁ n S) = σ (downExp m₂ n S)
  rw [hσadd]
  refine congrArg σ (funext fun i => ?_)
  by_cases hiS : i ∈ S
  · simp [downExp, hiS, Pi.add_apply]
  · simp only [downExp, hiS, ite_false, Pi.add_apply]
    omega

omit [Preadditive 𝒜] [HasFiniteProducts 𝒜] in
/-- **The downward transition at a level to itself is the identity**: its exponent vector is
zero. -/
theorem constDownNat_self (n : ℕ) :
    constDownNat σ hσ0 hσadd (le_refl n) = 𝟙 (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n) := by
  refine NatTrans.ext (funext fun S => ?_)
  change σ (downExp n n S) = 𝟙 Y
  rw [show downExp n n S = 0 from funext fun i => by simp [downExp]]
  exact hσ0

/-- The downward transition of Koszul complexes from a level to itself is the identity. -/
theorem constDownMap_self (n : ℕ) :
    constDownMap σ hσ0 hσadd (le_refl n) = 𝟙 (complex (constSystem σ hσ0 hσadd n)) := by
  rw [constDownMap, constDownNat_self, map_id]

/-- The downward transitions of Koszul complexes compose: going down from `m₂` to `m₁` and then
to `n` is going down from `m₂` to `n`. -/
theorem constDownMap_comp {m₁ m₂ n : ℕ} (h₁ : m₁ ≤ m₂) (h₂ : n ≤ m₁) :
    constDownMap σ hσ0 hσadd h₁ ≫ constDownMap σ hσ0 hσadd h₂ =
      constDownMap σ hσ0 hσadd (h₂.trans h₁) := by
  rw [constDownMap, constDownMap, constDownMap, ← map_comp, constDownNat_comp]

end Down

end CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech

/-! ## The identity of a finite product, decomposed -/

namespace CategoryTheory.Limits.Pi

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [Preadditive C] [HasFiniteBiproducts C]
  {ι : Type} [Fintype ι] (f : ι → C)

/-- The inclusion of a factor into a finite product, through the comparison of the product with
the biproduct. -/
def biproductIota (i : ι) : f i ⟶ ∏ᶜ f :=
  biproduct.ι f i ≫ (biproduct.isoProduct f).hom

/-- **The identity of a finite product is the sum of the composites projection-inclusion.** This
is `CategoryTheory.Limits.biproduct.total`, transported to the product. -/
theorem total_biproductIota : ∑ i, Pi.π f i ≫ biproductIota f i = 𝟙 (∏ᶜ f) := by
  have h : ∀ i, Pi.π f i = (biproduct.isoProduct f).inv ≫ biproduct.π f i := fun i => by
    rw [Iso.eq_inv_comp, biproduct.isoProduct_hom, Pi.lift_comp_π]
  calc ∑ i, Pi.π f i ≫ biproductIota f i
      = ∑ i, ((biproduct.isoProduct f).inv ≫ (biproduct.π f i ≫ biproduct.ι f i)) ≫
          (biproduct.isoProduct f).hom := by
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
        rw [biproductIota, h i]
        simp only [Category.assoc]
    _ = ((biproduct.isoProduct f).inv ≫ ∑ i, biproduct.π f i ≫ biproduct.ι f i) ≫
          (biproduct.isoProduct f).hom := by
        rw [Preadditive.comp_sum, Preadditive.sum_comp]
    _ = 𝟙 (∏ᶜ f) := by rw [biproduct.total, Category.comp_id, Iso.inv_hom_id]

end CategoryTheory.Limits.Pi

/-! ## A range bound from a decomposition of the identity -/

namespace Stacks.KoszulProZero

/-- **A map whose components are scalars from an ideal has its range inside that ideal times the
target.** The identity of the target is given as a finite sum of composites `π i ≫ ι i`, which is
what `CategoryTheory.Limits.Pi.total_biproductIota` supplies for a finite product. -/
theorem range_le_ideal_smul_of_total {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {ι : Type}
    {P Q : ModuleCat.{u} A} {R : ι → ModuleCat.{u} A} (I : Ideal A) (ψ : P ⟶ Q) (s : Finset ι)
    (pr : ∀ i, Q ⟶ R i) (inc : ∀ i, R i ⟶ Q)
    (htot : ∑ i ∈ s, pr i ≫ inc i = 𝟙 Q)
    (c : ι → A) (hc : ∀ i ∈ s, c i ∈ I) (χ : ∀ i, P ⟶ R i)
    (hψ : ∀ i ∈ s, ψ ≫ pr i = c i • χ i) :
    LinearMap.range ψ.hom ≤ I • (⊤ : Submodule A Q) := by
  rintro y ⟨x, rfl⟩
  have h1 : ψ = ∑ i ∈ s, (c i • χ i) ≫ inc i := by
    rw [← Category.comp_id ψ, ← htot, Preadditive.comp_sum]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i hi => ?_
    rw [← Category.assoc, hψ i hi]
  have h2 : ψ.hom x = ∑ i ∈ s, c i • (inc i).hom ((χ i).hom x) := by
    rw [h1, ModuleCat.hom_sum]
    simp only [ModuleCat.hom_comp, ModuleCat.hom_smul]
    rw [LinearMap.sum_apply]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by simp
  rw [h2]
  exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i hi =>
    Submodule.smul_mem_smul (hc i hi) Submodule.mem_top

/-! ## The subset-product Koszul complex of a module over a commutative ring -/

section ModuleSide

open CategoryTheory.AlternatingCech AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (a : Fin r → A) (N : ModuleCat.{u} A)

/-- **The monomial multiplications of an `A`-module**, as a multiplicative family of
endomorphisms: at the exponent vector `e` it is multiplication by `∏_i a_i^{e_i}`. -/
@[reducible] def smulFam : (Fin r → ℕ) → (N ⟶ N) := fun e => moduleKoszulValue a e • 𝟙 N

/-- The monomial multiplication at the zero exponent vector is the identity. -/
theorem smulFam_zero : smulFam a N 0 = 𝟙 N := by
  change moduleKoszulValue a 0 • 𝟙 N = 𝟙 N
  rw [moduleKoszulValue_zero, one_smul]

/-- The monomial multiplications are multiplicative: the composite at `e` and `e'` is the
multiplication at `e + e'`. -/
theorem smulFam_add (e e' : Fin r → ℕ) :
    smulFam a N e ≫ smulFam a N e' = smulFam a N (e + e') := by
  change (moduleKoszulValue a e • 𝟙 N) ≫ (moduleKoszulValue a e' • 𝟙 N) =
    moduleKoszulValue a (e + e') • 𝟙 N
  rw [Linear.smul_comp, Category.id_comp, smul_smul, moduleKoszulValue_add]

/-- The constant Koszul system of the monomial multiplications of `N`. It is definitionally
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleKoszulPowerFunctor`, and is reducible so that its value at a
subset is recognised as `N` without an `eqToHom`. -/
@[reducible] def modSystem (n : ℕ) : Finset (Fin r) ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A :=
  constSystem (smulFam a N) (smulFam_zero a N) (smulFam_add a N) n

/-- `modSystem` is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleKoszulPowerFunctor`. -/
theorem modSystem_eq (n : ℕ) : modSystem a N n = moduleKoszulPowerFunctor a N n := rfl

/-- **The Koszul complex on the `(n+1)`-st powers of `a_1, …, a_r` with coefficients in `N`.**
Definitionally `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleKoszulPowerComplex`. -/
@[reducible] def modComplex (n : ℕ) : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ :=
  complex (modSystem a N n)

/-- `modComplex` is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleKoszulPowerComplex`. -/
theorem modComplex_eq (n : ℕ) : modComplex a N n = moduleKoszulPowerComplex a N n := rfl

/-- The monomial concentrated at the single index `j` is the `(n+1)`-st power of `a j`. -/
theorem moduleKoszulValue_singleExp (j : Fin r) (n : ℕ) :
    moduleKoszulValue a (singleExp j n) = a j ^ (n + 1) := by
  change (∏ i, a i ^ singleExp j n i) = a j ^ (n + 1)
  refine (Finset.prod_eq_single j (fun i _ hij => ?_)
    (fun h => absurd (Finset.mem_univ j) h)).trans ?_
  · rw [show singleExp j n i = 0 from ite_eq_right hij, pow_zero]
  · rw [show singleExp j n j = n + 1 from ite_eq_left rfl]

/-- Multiplication by the monomial `∏_i a_i^{e_i}` on the Koszul complex is the scalar action of
that monomial. -/
theorem constSmulMap_modComplex (n : ℕ) (e : Fin r → ℕ) :
    constSmulMap (smulFam a N) (smulFam_zero a N) (smulFam_add a N) n e =
      moduleKoszulValue a e • 𝟙 (modComplex a N n) := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun q => ?_
  change constSmulTerm (smulFam a N) (smulFam_zero a N) (smulFam_add a N) n e q =
    moduleKoszulValue a e • 𝟙 (term (modSystem a N n) q)
  refine Pi.hom_ext _ _ fun B => ?_
  rw [constSmulTerm_comp_pi, Linear.smul_comp, Category.id_comp]
  change _ ≫ (moduleKoszulValue a e • 𝟙 N) = _
  rw [Linear.comp_smul, Category.comp_id]

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0663] with coefficients, in the subset-product model.** The ideal generated by
`a_1^{n+1}, …, a_r^{n+1}` annihilates every cohomology module of the Koszul complex on those
powers with coefficients in `N`. -/
theorem span_le_annihilator_homology_modComplex (n : ℕ) (p : ℤ) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => a i ^ (n + 1)) ≤
      Module.annihilator A ((modComplex a N n).homology p) := by
  refine Ideal.span_le.2 ?_
  rintro c ⟨j, rfl⟩
  refine Module.mem_annihilator.mpr fun x => ?_
  have hzero : HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
      (a j ^ (n + 1) • 𝟙 (modComplex a N n)) p = 0 := by
    rw [← moduleKoszulValue_singleExp a j n, ← constSmulMap_modComplex a N n (singleExp j n),
      (constSmulNullHomotopic (smulFam a N) (smulFam_zero a N) (smulFam_add a N)
        j n).homologyMap_eq p, HomologicalComplex.homologyMap_zero]
  rw [HomologicalComplex.homologyMap_smul_id] at hzero
  simpa only [ModuleCat.hom_smul, ModuleCat.hom_id, LinearMap.smul_apply, LinearMap.id_apply,
    ModuleCat.hom_zero, LinearMap.zero_apply] using
    congrArg (fun φ : (modComplex a N n).homology p ⟶ (modComplex a N n).homology p => φ.hom x)
      hzero

/-- **The transition map of the module Koszul complexes from the `(m+1)`-st down to the
`(n+1)`-st powers.** -/
def modDown {m n : ℕ} (hnm : n ≤ m) : modComplex a N m ⟶ modComplex a N n :=
  constDownMap (smulFam a N) (smulFam_zero a N) (smulFam_add a N) hnm

/-- A subset of `Fin r` of cardinality less than `r` misses an index. -/
theorem exists_notMem_of_card_lt {p : ℤ} (hp : p < r) (S : Idx r p) : ∃ i : Fin r, i ∉ S.1 := by
  by_contra hcon
  have huniv : S.1 = Finset.univ :=
    Finset.eq_univ_iff_forall.2 fun i => not_not.1 fun h => hcon ⟨i, h⟩
  have hcard := S.2
  rw [huniv, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_fin] at hcard
  omega

/-- **The image of the downward transition in a degree below the top lies in `Jᵏ` times the
term**, where `J` is the ideal generated by the `(n+1)`-st powers. In degree `p < r` every
indexing subset misses an index, so every component of the transition is a monomial divisible by
`a_i^{(n+1)k}` for some `i`. -/
theorem range_modDown_le_ideal_smul (n k : ℕ) {m : ℕ} (hm : m = n + (n + 1) * k)
    (hnm : n ≤ m) (p : ℤ) (hp : p < r) :
    LinearMap.range ((modDown a N hnm).f p).hom ≤
      (Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => a i ^ (n + 1))) ^ k •
        (⊤ : Submodule A ((modComplex a N n).X p)) := by
  classical
  change LinearMap.range ((modDown a N hnm).f p).hom ≤
      (Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => a i ^ (n + 1))) ^ k •
        (⊤ : Submodule A ↥(term (modSystem a N n) p))
  refine range_le_ideal_smul_of_total _ _ Finset.univ
    (fun S : Idx r p => Pi.π (fun T : Idx r p => (modSystem a N n).obj T.1) S)
    (fun S : Idx r p => Pi.biproductIota (fun T : Idx r p => (modSystem a N n).obj T.1) S)
    (Pi.total_biproductIota _)
    (fun S : Idx r p => moduleKoszulValue a (downExp m n S.1)) (fun S _ => ?_)
    (fun S : Idx r p => Pi.π (fun T : Idx r p => (modSystem a N m).obj T.1) S) (fun S _ => ?_)
  · obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := exists_notMem_of_card_lt hp S
    have hpow : a i ^ ((n + (n + 1) * k) - n) ∈
        (Ideal.span (Set.range fun j => a j ^ (n + 1))) ^ k :=
      NoetherianKoszulProIso.power_generator_mem_span_pow a n k i
    have hval : downExp m n S.1 i = (n + (n + 1) * k) - n := by
      rw [downExp, ite_eq_right hi, hm]
    change (∏ j, a j ^ downExp m n S.1 j) ∈ _
    rw [← Finset.mul_prod_erase Finset.univ (fun j => a j ^ downExp m n S.1 j)
      (Finset.mem_univ i), hval]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hpow
  · have h1 : (modDown a N hnm).f p ≫
        Pi.π (fun T : Idx r p => (modSystem a N n).obj T.1) S =
        Pi.π (fun T : Idx r p => (modSystem a N m).obj T.1) S ≫ smulFam a N (downExp m n S.1) :=
      mapX_comp_pi
        (constDownNat (smulFam a N) (smulFam_zero a N) (smulFam_add a N) hnm) S
    rw [h1]
    change _ ≫ (moduleKoszulValue a (downExp m n S.1) • 𝟙 N) = _
    rw [Linear.comp_smul, Category.comp_id]
    rfl

/-- **The property that a map of complexes of modules carries the cocycles of its source in a
degree into the coboundaries of its target.** For a map of short complexes of modules it is
equivalent to the vanishing of the induced map on cohomology, and unlike that vanishing it
mentions no subquotient, which is what makes it transport along a flat base change. -/
def CocyclesIntoCoboundaries {C D : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ} (φ : C ⟶ D) (p : ℤ) :
    Prop :=
  ∀ x : C.X p, (C.d p (p + 1)).hom x = 0 →
    (φ.f p).hom x ∈ LinearMap.range ((D.d (p - 1) p)).hom

/-- **The cocycle-into-coboundary property is inherited by a precomposite.** A chain map carries
cocycles to cocycles, so if `φ` has the property then so does `ψ ≫ φ`. -/
theorem cocyclesIntoCoboundaries_comp {B C D : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} A) ℤ}
    (ψ : B ⟶ C) (φ : C ⟶ D) (p : ℤ) (h : CocyclesIntoCoboundaries φ p) :
    CocyclesIntoCoboundaries (ψ ≫ φ) p := by
  intro x hx
  have hc := congrArg (fun χ : B.X p ⟶ C.X (p + 1) => χ.hom x) (ψ.comm p (p + 1))
  simp only [ModuleCat.hom_comp, LinearMap.comp_apply] at hc
  refine h ((ψ.f p).hom x) ?_
  rw [hc, hx, map_zero]

/-- **The property persists at later levels.** If the transition from level `m₁` down to level
`n` carries cocycles into coboundaries then so does the transition from any later level `m₂`,
because the latter factors through the former. -/
theorem cocyclesIntoCoboundaries_modDown_of_le {m₁ m₂ n : ℕ} (h₁ : m₁ ≤ m₂) (hnm₁ : n ≤ m₁)
    (p : ℤ) (h : CocyclesIntoCoboundaries (modDown a N hnm₁) p) :
    CocyclesIntoCoboundaries (modDown a N (hnm₁.trans h₁)) p := by
  rw [modDown, ← constDownMap_comp (smulFam a N) (smulFam_zero a N) (smulFam_add a N) h₁ hnm₁]
  exact cocyclesIntoCoboundaries_comp _ _ p h

/-- **The positive Koszul cohomology of the power tower of a finite module over a Noetherian ring
is pro-zero**, in the subset-product model: in every degree `p` below the top degree `r` and at
every level `n` there is a later level `m` at which the downward transition carries the cocycles
of level `m` into the coboundaries of level `n`.

This is the Artin–Rees input of [Stacks, Tag 0921] with coefficients. -/
theorem exists_modDown_cocyclesIntoCoboundaries [IsNoetherianRing A] [Module.Finite A N]
    (n : ℕ) (p : ℤ) (hp : p < r) :
    ∃ (m : ℕ) (hnm : n ≤ m), CocyclesIntoCoboundaries (modDown a N hnm) p := by
  classical
  have hnext : (ComplexShape.up ℤ).next p = p + 1 := ComplexShape.next_eq' _ rfl
  have hprev : (ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev p = p - 1 :=
    ComplexShape.prev_eq' (ComplexShape.up ℤ) (i := p) (j := p - 1) (by change p - 1 + 1 = p; omega)
  have hfin : Module.Finite A (((modComplex a N n).sc p).X₂ : Type u) :=
    Module.Finite.equiv
      (ModuleCat.piIsoPi (fun T : Idx r p => (modSystem a N n).obj T.1)).symm.toLinearEquiv
  have hann : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => a i ^ (n + 1)) ≤
      Module.annihilator A ((modComplex a N n).sc p).homology :=
    span_le_annihilator_homology_modComplex a N n p
  have hJB := NoetherianKoszulProIso.ideal_smul_ker_le_range_of_annihilator
    ((modComplex a N n).sc p) (Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => a i ^ (n + 1))) hann
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := NoetherianKoszulProIso.artinRees_cycles_bound
    (Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => a i ^ (n + 1)))
    (LinearMap.ker (((modComplex a N n).sc p).g).hom)
    (LinearMap.range (((modComplex a N n).sc p).f).hom) hJB
  have hnm' : n ≤ n + (n + 1) * k := by omega
  refine ⟨n + (n + 1) * k, hnm', fun x hx => ?_⟩
  have hx' : (((modComplex a N (n + (n + 1) * k)).sc p).g).hom x = 0 := by
    change ((modComplex a N (n + (n + 1) * k)).d p ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).next p)).hom x = 0
    rwa [hnext]
  have h : (((modComplex a N n).sc p).g).hom (((modDown a N hnm').f p).hom x) =
      ((modDown a N hnm').f ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).next p)).hom
        ((((modComplex a N (n + (n + 1) * k)).sc p).g).hom x) :=
    congrArg (fun φ : ((modComplex a N (n + (n + 1) * k)).sc p).X₂ ⟶
      (modComplex a N n).X ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).next p) => φ.hom x)
      ((modDown a N hnm').comm p ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).next p))
  have hmem : ((modDown a N hnm').f p).hom x ∈
      LinearMap.range ((modComplex a N n).d ((ComplexShape.up ℤ).prev p) p).hom :=
    hk ⟨range_modDown_le_ideal_smul a N n k rfl hnm' p hp ⟨x, rfl⟩,
      LinearMap.mem_ker.mpr (by rw [h, hx']; exact map_zero _)⟩
  rwa [hprev] at hmem

end ModuleSide

end Stacks.KoszulProZero

